invariant: INV-34
file: x25519_wide.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh x25519_wide_tail
reason: carry_columns adds column 0's carry in 128 bits because the multiply
  contract cannot show that column 0 is under 2^115: it holds four products
  of a word by 19 times a word, and over operand words under 2^54 the
  contract bounds their sum by 2^115 + 2^108 (docs/decisions.md 152). The
  real column is under 2^114.3, so the values stay right and the vectors
  pass. Narrowed to a word through column_carry, the multiply by 2^13 wraps
  under the contract, and x25519_wide_tail, whose operands reach 2^54,
  reports it.

--- old
    t1 += t0 >> WORD_BITS;
    t2 += column_carry(t1);
--- new
    t1 += column_carry(t0);
    t2 += column_carry(t1);
